WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.314
Welcome to OurWater.

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:08.098
After this video you can ask for a station's
data, answer requests about your stations,

00:00:08.218 --> 00:00:12.370
tidy your messages, and keep a list of your
favourite stations.

00:00:13.183 --> 00:00:18.799
Sometimes you need data from a station that is
not yours, or a neighbour asks for yours.

00:00:18.919 --> 00:00:21.391
Requests is where that happens.

00:00:21.511 --> 00:00:24.103
Click Account, then Requests.

00:00:24.917 --> 00:00:26.885
Along the top are tabs.

00:00:27.005 --> 00:00:29.525
Request data is always here.

00:00:29.645 --> 00:00:33.797
Station transfers and Privacy appear when you
have something in them.

00:00:34.617 --> 00:00:38.457
Here you ask for a station's measurements as a
spreadsheet file.

00:00:38.577 --> 00:00:41.649
Whoever looks after that station decides.

00:00:41.769 --> 00:00:45.393
For your own station, the file is ready at
once.

00:00:46.217 --> 00:00:50.633
Start with the station code, from the
station's page or its label.

00:00:50.753 --> 00:00:53.777
I am asking for a rain gauge at a school.

00:00:54.583 --> 00:00:56.455
Dates are optional.

00:00:56.575 --> 00:00:59.527
I ask only from the first of September.

00:00:59.647 --> 00:01:02.647
Leave both empty to ask for everything.

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:06.522
In Purpose, say why you want the data.

00:01:06.642 --> 00:01:09.450
A short reason helps the owner say yes.

00:01:10.283 --> 00:01:12.155
Click Request data.

00:01:12.275 --> 00:01:14.675
A green message says it is sent.

00:01:14.795 --> 00:01:17.555
The answer will arrive in Messages.

00:01:18.383 --> 00:01:21.743
Your request appears below, marked pending.

00:01:21.863 --> 00:01:23.735
It waits for the owner.

00:01:23.855 --> 00:01:25.727
Changed your mind?

00:01:25.847 --> 00:01:27.839
Click Cancel request.

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:32.970
This list also shows requests from others
about your stations.

00:01:33.090 --> 00:01:35.898
The card says who asks, and why.

00:01:36.018 --> 00:01:38.634
Approve gives them a download link.

00:01:38.754 --> 00:01:40.626
Decline says no.

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:43.322
I click Approve.

00:01:43.442 --> 00:01:47.642
The person gets a message with a download link
that lasts two days.

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:50.874
For this one I click Decline.

00:01:50.994 --> 00:01:53.826
The person gets a short message saying no.

00:01:54.650 --> 00:01:58.010
Later, the organisation admin answers.

00:01:58.130 --> 00:02:02.426
One request is approved, with a Download CSV
button.

00:02:02.546 --> 00:02:06.578
The other is declined, so there is nothing to
download.

00:02:07.383 --> 00:02:10.119
A station can also change hands.

00:02:10.239 --> 00:02:15.279
When something waits for your answer, Requests
opens on this tab by itself.

00:02:15.399 --> 00:02:20.919
People join an organisation by invitation, so
no join requests appear.

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:24.270
A neighbour offers me his pump house.

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:28.038
Click Accept station to look after it, or
Decline.

00:02:28.158 --> 00:02:30.774
Nothing changes until you choose.

00:02:31.583 --> 00:02:33.503
This card is mine.

00:02:33.623 --> 00:02:36.839
I offered my rain gauge to the organisation.

00:02:36.959 --> 00:02:39.791
It waits for them, and I can cancel.

00:02:40.617 --> 00:02:44.721
The Privacy tab follows your requests to make
a station private.

00:02:44.841 --> 00:02:48.441
A Super Admin decides, so it says Waiting.

00:02:48.561 --> 00:02:50.913
You can cancel while it waits.

00:02:51.717 --> 00:02:54.285
Every answer lands in Messages.

00:02:54.405 --> 00:02:57.717
The number beside it counts what you have not
read yet.

00:02:58.550 --> 00:03:00.806
Each line is one message.

00:03:00.926 --> 00:03:03.470
A dot and bold letters mean new.

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:07.166
Under each title are its kind, and who sent
it.

00:03:07.983 --> 00:03:09.951
Click a message to read it.

00:03:10.071 --> 00:03:14.487
Opening it marks it read, so the dot goes and
the number drops.

00:03:14.607 --> 00:03:18.447
This one holds your download link and an Open
Requests button.

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:21.482
Looking for an older message?

00:03:21.602 --> 00:03:23.546
Type a word in Search.

00:03:23.666 --> 00:03:26.018
Only matching messages stay.

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:28.722
Need help?

00:03:28.842 --> 00:03:30.714
Click Message admin.

00:03:30.834 --> 00:03:36.162
Send to lets you choose the OurWater admin, or
your own organisation's admin.

00:03:36.983 --> 00:03:41.231
Write a short subject and your message, then
click Send to admin.

00:03:41.351 --> 00:03:43.727
A green message says it was sent.

00:03:44.550 --> 00:03:48.822
Mark all read clears every dot at once, and
the number too.

00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:53.178
To delete one message, open it and click
Delete.

00:03:53.298 --> 00:03:56.250
OurWater asks you to confirm first.

00:03:57.083 --> 00:03:59.675
I confirm, and it is gone.

00:03:59.795 --> 00:04:02.099
It is deleted only for you.

00:04:02.917 --> 00:04:06.541
Clear read deletes every message you have
already read.

00:04:06.661 --> 00:04:09.757
It asks first, and tells you how many.

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:12.863
Now the inbox is empty.

00:04:12.983 --> 00:04:16.055
New answers will appear here by themselves.

00:04:16.883 --> 00:04:19.739
A favourite is a station you visit often.

00:04:19.859 --> 00:04:24.851
In My stations, search for it, click it, then
click Add to favourites.

00:04:24.971 --> 00:04:27.323
The button then reads Favourited.

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:30.598
Favourites is in the Account menu.

00:04:30.718 --> 00:04:35.254
Each station shows its name, its code, and the
day you added it.

00:04:36.083 --> 00:04:38.723
On a long list, type in Search.

00:04:38.843 --> 00:04:41.219
It looks at the name and the code.

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:44.738
Remove takes a station off the list.

00:04:44.858 --> 00:04:48.914
The station itself is not deleted, only the
shortcut.

00:04:49.717 --> 00:04:52.213
Click a name to open the station.

00:04:52.333 --> 00:04:56.053
OurWater quietly remembers every station you
open.

00:04:56.883 --> 00:05:01.803
Recent activity lists the stations you opened
lately, newest first.

00:05:01.923 --> 00:05:04.155
Click one to go straight back.

00:05:04.275 --> 00:05:06.315
There is nothing to set up.

00:05:07.117 --> 00:05:11.893
That is Requests, Messages, Favourites and
Recent activity.

00:05:12.013 --> 00:05:14.677
Thanks for helping look after our water.
